failure the step's refusal; each method is one step, which holds where calls don't interleave (one at a time, or under a Semaphore of 1)","make makes an object of functions: its state is what they close over (jobs_items, jobs_head, jobs_tail, jobs_open, workers_taken, workers_held, spent, __gdp_pc, __gdp_work_cost), its arguments the params","a transaction that waits (STM.check, STM.retry, Effect.txRetry) is not taken until a TRef it read changes: the rule refuses the request (it is taken later as a new one)","submit_cost: an integer (the code takes any whole number)","workers_taken: an integer (a step may take it below 0, or it starts there)","workers_held: an integer (a step may take it below 0, or it starts there)","spent: an integer (a step may take it below 0, or it starts there)","__gdp_work_cost: an integer (a step may take it below 0, or it starts there)","backlog_result: an integer (a step may take it below 0, or it starts there)","lemma proven, beside every law: workers: what its fibers hold is never below nothing","lemma not proven (left out): workers: no fiber gives back more permits than it took"],"laws":[{"name":"every job waiting costs 1 to 10","expr":"forall k in jobs_items: (jobs_head <= k and k < jobs_tail) implies (1 <= jobs_items[k] and jobs_items[k] <= 10)","where":"effect-pool.ts:9","kind":"law","verdict":"proven","ms":542},{"name":"the work done never goes negative","expr":"spent >= 0","where":"effect-pool.ts:10","kind":"law","verdict":"proven","ms":577},{"name":"no permit is given back that wasn't taken","expr":"workers_taken >= 0","where":"effect-pool.ts:11","kind":"law","verdict":"proven","ms":603}]}]},"exit":0,"signal":null,"wallMs":68274.12685599999,"resources":{"telemetryVersion":2,"label":"trace-3-unshared-rows","strictSeconds":300,"before":{"at":"2026-11-10T00:50:59.184Z","uptime":"2069.06 13875.30","memory":{"MemTotal":16375780,"MemFree":9821524,"MemAvailable":13744952,"Buffers":176640,"Cached":3922188,"SwapCached":0,"Active":2308648,